From dee332cb80601cf91abe99af3510ddc86a2a1891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Toemmsen96 <147745097+Toemmsen96@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:19:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: samsung-s6e8aa5x01-ams497hy01: Add brightness
 control

The generated driver registers no backlight device, so the panel always
runs with the 360 cd gamma/AID/ELVSS values of the init sequence and
user space cannot change the brightness.

Add a raw backlight device (0-255, default 128) unless a backlight is
described in DT, and implement the brightness update of the Samsung
vendor kernel for the Galaxy J5 (SM-J500F):

 - The level selects one of 62 candela steps (5-360 cd) through
   samsung,candela_map_table_revA of the vendor panel dtsi. Level 0 is
   the lowest step, the panel is never switched off.

 - For that step the update sends, with level 1 key (0xf0 0x5a 0x5a)
   enabled, in the order of mdss_samsung_normal_brightenss_packet_set():
   AID (0xb2) from samsung,aid_tx_cmds_revA/C via aid_map_table,
   ACL 15% (0x55 0x02, 0xb5 0x50) below level 255 and ACL off
   (0x55 0x00, 0xb5 0x40) at 255 as done by
   samsung,samsung_change_acl_by_brightness, ELVSS (0xb6 0xbc xx) from
   samsung,elvss_tx_cmds_revA via smart_acl_elvss_map_table, the
   temperature (0xb8 parameter 8, fixed to 20 degrees as the vendor
   kernel has no other source either), the low luminance ELVSS value
   (0xb6 parameter 22: the OTP value above 29 cd, 0x07/0x05 below), the
   gamma (0xca) and the gamma update (0xf7 0x03).

 - The gamma for each step is generated with the vendor "smart dimming"
   algorithm (ss_dsi_smart_dimming_S6E8AA5X01_AMS497HY01.[ch]): the
   per-panel MTP gamma offsets (0xc8, 33 bytes) are read once, the
   panel's gray scale voltages are derived from them and the reference
   gamma, and for every candela step the gamma register values are
   computed from a 2.0 gamma curve at the step's base luminance,
   corrected by the vendor gradation and RGB offset tables and by the
   MTP offsets. The port keeps the vendor integer arithmetic, and its
   output was checked to be identical to the vendor code for 3000
   random MTP inputs on both panel revisions.

Like the vendor kernel, the panel ID (0xda-0xdc), the ELVSS OTP value
(0xb6 offset 0x15) and the MTP are read once before sleep out, using the
0xb0 offset register and reads of at most 7 bytes. The third ID byte
selects the panel revision: 0x02 uses the revA AID and smart dimming
tables, anything else the revC ones. If the ID cannot be read, revA is
used. If the MTP cannot be read, the reference (360 cd) gamma is kept
and only AID/ELVSS/ACL follow the brightness, which still covers about
12-360 cd.

The init sequence is unchanged. The requested level is applied after it
and before display on, so it survives a power cycle of the panel.
Updates while the panel is on are sent in HS mode like the vendor
kernel does, and updates while the panel is off or the backlight is
blanked are only cached.

